# Keep the build context to what the image actually needs.
# node_modules is critical: without it `COPY . .` would overwrite the Linux dependencies installed inside the image
# with whatever the host has (a macOS or Windows tree), and a local config.json/.env would be baked into the image.
node_modules
.pnpm-store
.git
.gitignore
.github
# Credentials: the exact names were the only ones kept out, so `.env.local` / `config.local.json` / a private key
# sitting in the working tree were baked into the image layer that `COPY . .` creates.
# The package-manager and git credential files are the same class and were still missing: `.npmrc` (where a pnpm/npm
# registry token lives), `.netrc`, `.git-credentials`, an SSH private key and a PKCS#12 bundle were copied into the image
# and pushed to Docker Hub, where a layer stays pullable. `.pnpmrc`/`.yarnrc*` carry registry auth too.
.env
.env.*
config.json
config.*.json
.npmrc
.pnpmrc
.yarnrc
.yarnrc.yml
.netrc
_netrc
.git-credentials
id_rsa*
id_dsa*
id_ecdsa*
id_ed25519*
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore
*.jks
*.pem
*.key
*.log
.DS_Store
.vscode
.idea
# The smoke suite needs a stub backend and a writable port; it is not part of the runtime image
test
# Documentation is not part of the runtime image either: it was shipped into /app (AGENTS.md alone is tens of KB) and
# nothing in the container reads it. LICENSE stays, because it has to travel with the code.
AGENTS.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
README.md
docker/README.md
